	abstract = {The distribution of the Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) test statistic has been widely studied under the assumption that the underlying theoretical cumulative distribution function (CDF), F (x), is continuous. However, there are many real-life applications in which ﬁtting discrete or mixed distributions is required. Nevertheless, due to inherent diﬃculties, the distribution of the KS statistic when F (x) has jump discontinuities has been studied to a much lesser extent and no exact and eﬃcient computational methods have been proposed in the literature.},
